  "abstract": "This experiment tests a novel optimization paradigm, Container Relaxation Optimization (CRO), designed to overcome the limitations of hard boundary constraints. It first optimizes a multi-start jitter search in a slightly expanded container ('[-0.1, 1.1]') without boundary constraints, allowing the packing to find its natural, high-density structure. The resulting optimal packing is then uniformly scaled and normalized to fit the unit square. This hypothesis challenges the fundamental assumption of a fixed container during optimization and aims to discover superior structural classes inaccessible to traditional methods.",
